RISC OS: install the crash report first thing.

Calls YsRiscOsInstallErrorReport() (ysce_public patch 04) at the start of
the game (BeforeEverything) and the console server (main), so a data abort
or RISC OS error writes "RISC OS error &...: ..." and a backtrace to
stderr.

For YSCE 231e711. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-ysflight.

diff --git a/src/main/fsmain.cpp b/src/main/fsmain.cpp
index 4ef75f4..ccb100b 100644
--- a/src/main/fsmain.cpp
+++ b/src/main/fsmain.cpp
@@ -117,6 +117,9 @@ FsLazyWindowApplication::FsLazyWindowApplication()
 
 /* virtual */ void FsLazyWindowApplication::BeforeEverything(int ac,char *av[])
 {
+#ifdef __riscos__
+	YsRiscOsInstallErrorReport();
+#endif
 	printf("YSFLIGHT\n");
 	printf("VERSION %d\n",YSFLIGHT_VERSION);
 	printf("YFSVERSION %d\n",YSFLIGHT_YFSVERSION);
diff --git a/src/main_consvr/fsmainsvr.cpp b/src/main_consvr/fsmainsvr.cpp
index 04f086f..109b11a 100644
--- a/src/main_consvr/fsmainsvr.cpp
+++ b/src/main_consvr/fsmainsvr.cpp
@@ -108,6 +108,9 @@ extern FsScreenMessage fsConsole;
 
 int main(int ac,char *av[])
 {
+#ifdef __riscos__
+	YsRiscOsInstallErrorReport();
+#endif
 	ForceLink();
 
 	printf("YSFLIGHT\n");
